A solutions architect reviews this CloudFormation resource fragment. WorkQueue is an AWS::SQS::Queue resource declared elsewhere in the same template.

{
  "EventTopic": {
    "Type": "AWS::SNS::Topic",
    "Properties": {
      "Subscription": [
        {
          "Protocol": "sqs",
          "Endpoint": {
            "Fn::GetAtt": [
              "WorkQueue",
              "Arn"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

What does the fragment declare?

An IAM user in an AWS Organizations member account cannot create an S3 bucket. Root and OU SCPs permit the action. The following is the only SCP attached directly to this account:

{"Version":"2012-10-17","Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Action":["cloudtrail:*","iam:*"],"Resource":"*"}]}

The user has this identity policy:

{"Version":"2012-10-17","Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Action":"s3:*","Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::*"},{"Effect":"Deny","NotAction":"s3:*","NotResource":"arn:aws:s3:::*"}]}

No other policy or control changes this evaluation. Why is s3:CreateBucket denied?

An organization uses SCPs to limit a departmental OU to EC2 and S3. The following SCP replaces FullAWSAccess at that OU; SCPs at every other level on the account path permit these actions.

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "ec2:*",
        "s3:*"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}

A newly created IAM user in a member account has no identity policies or group memberships. Its CreateBucket request is denied. Investigation finds no applicable explicit deny or other permission restriction.

What explains the result?
